{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/tutorials\/silo\/buildingad6diceroller"]}],"hierarchy":{"modules":[{"projects":[{"sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Creating-the-Data-Source","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Building-the-Dice-View","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Rolling-Automatically","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessment"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/Your-First-Data-Source"},{"projects":[{"sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Setting-Up-the-Dice-Service","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Choosing-the-Right-Refresh-Policy","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Adding-a-Second-Dependency","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Bridging-Streams-to-SwiftUI","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Building-the-Roll-View","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessment"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/Reactive-Dependencies"}],"paths":[["doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo","doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/$volume","doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/Your-First-Data-Source"],["doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo"]],"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo"},"kind":"project","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"category":"Silo","title":"Rolling a D6","categoryPathComponent":"Silo","role":"project"},"sections":[{"kind":"hero","title":"Rolling a D6","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial, you will build a D6 dice roller using Silo. The fetch is a single line — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int.random(in: 1...6)"},{"type":"text","text":" — so every concept you encounter is focused on Silo, with no boilerplate distractions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You will create a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/DataSource","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" backed by a random number, drive a SwiftUI view from its reactive stream, wire up a Roll button, and configure the die to roll itself automatically while the view is on screen."}]}],"chapter":"Your First Data Source","estimatedTimeInMinutes":15},{"kind":"tasks","tasks":[{"anchor":"Creating-the-Data-Source","contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a "},{"code":"DiceRoller","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" service that holds a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/DataSource"},{"type":"text","text":" for the last roll. Because the current roll may be absent before the die is first rolled, "},{"code":"Int?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the appropriate type — "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" means “not yet rolled.”"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Optional","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is one of Silo’s built-in empty types, so no "},{"code":"emptyValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure is needed. The source starts as "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and updates to a number each time "},{"code":"refresh()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is called."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"title":"Creating the Data Source","stepsSection":[{"media":null,"caption":[],"runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","code":"DiceRoller-01.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create "},{"code":"DiceRoller.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Define an empty "},{"code":"DiceRoller","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" class marked "},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with a "},{"code":"shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" singleton."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"media":null,"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"Task.sleep","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" delay is artificial — it simulates a slow fetch so the "},{"code":"ProgressView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" added in the next section remains visible during development. A real fetch would call a network API here instead."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","code":"DiceRoller-02.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"code":"lastRoll","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/DataSource"},{"type":"text","text":". The fetch closure returns "},{"code":"Int.random(in: 1...6)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"code":"onError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handler returns "},{"code":".keep","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so that any error preserves the previous roll value."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"anchor":"Building-the-Dice-View","contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Subscribe to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo\/DataSource\/valueWithState"},{"type":"text","text":" in a SwiftUI view. This stream delivers a snapshot on every change — value or loading state — so one subscription drives both the roll display and the "},{"code":"ProgressView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":".task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier iterates the stream for as long as the view is on screen. When the view disappears, the task is cancelled automatically — a behaviour that becomes relevant when auto-roll is introduced in the next section."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"title":"Building the Dice View","stepsSection":[{"media":null,"caption":[],"runtimePreview":"DiceView-01.png","type":"step","code":"DiceView-01.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create "},{"code":"DiceView.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with a reference to "},{"code":"DiceRoller.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and a placeholder body."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"media":null,"caption":[],"runtimePreview":"DiceView-02.png","type":"step","code":"DiceView-02.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" properties for the current roll and loading state. In "},{"code":".task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", iterate "},{"code":"roller.lastRoll.valueWithState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and update state from each snapshot. Show the roll as a large number — "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" renders as "},{"code":"\"—\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" before the first roll — and a "},{"code":"ProgressView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" while the source is refreshing."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"media":null,"caption":[],"runtimePreview":"DiceView-03.png","type":"step","code":"DiceView-03.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a Roll button that calls "},{"code":"refresh(clear: true)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Passing "},{"code":"clear: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sets "},{"code":"lastRoll","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" back to "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" immediately, so the display returns to "},{"code":"\"—\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" while the next number is being generated — a clear visual cue that a new roll is in flight."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"anchor":"Rolling-Automatically","contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Chain "},{"code":".autoRefresh(.seconds(2))","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to roll the die automatically every two seconds while the view is visible. The timer is subscriber-driven: it starts when the first subscriber appears on "},{"code":"lastRoll.values","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and stops when the last one disappears."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because "},{"code":".task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"code":"DiceView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cancels when the view leaves the screen, the auto-roll timer stops automatically — no manual cleanup is required."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"title":"Rolling Automatically","stepsSection":[{"media":null,"caption":[],"runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","code":"DiceRoller-03.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Chain "},{"code":".autoRefresh(.seconds(2))","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" before "},{"code":".build()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The view requires no changes: the existing "},{"code":"valueWithState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" subscription picks up each automatic roll as it arrives."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]},{"kind":"assessments","assessments":[{"title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lastRoll"},{"text":" is typed as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DataSource<Int?>"},{"text":". What does ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" represent?","type":"text"}]}],"content":[],"choices":[{"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Errors are handled separately by the "},{"code":"onError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure, not encoded as "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value comes from Silo’s built-in empty state for "},{"code":"Optional","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" types — it simply means the source has never been fetched."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An error occurred during the last roll."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Optional","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is one of Silo’s built-in empty types. The source starts as "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and stays "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" until "},{"code":"refresh()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is first called — or after "},{"code":"refresh(clear: true)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" resets it while a new roll is in flight."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The die has not been rolled yet, or the value was cleared."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Auto-roll is configured via "},{"code":".autoRefresh()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on the builder, not encoded in the value type. "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" means the source has no value yet, regardless of whether auto-roll is on or off."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Auto-roll is disabled."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"multiple-choice"},{"title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh(clear: true)"},{"text":" and then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh(clear: true)"},{"text":" again immediately. How many rolls happen?","type":"text"}]}],"content":[],"choices":[{"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Concurrent "},{"code":"refresh()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" calls are deduplicated. The second caller joins the in-flight task started by the first and awaits its result — only one roll ever happens."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two rolls — one for each call."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Silo deduplicates concurrent refreshes. The second "},{"code":"refresh()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call detects an active task and awaits it instead of starting a new one. Both callers receive the same result."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One roll — the second call joins the in-flight task."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calls are deduplicated, not cancelled. The in-flight task runs to completion and both callers receive the result."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Zero rolls — the second call cancels the first."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"multiple-choice"},{"title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You configure ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".autoRefresh(.seconds(2))"},{"text":". The user navigates away and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiceView"},{"text":" disappears. What happens to the timer?","type":"text"}]}],"content":[],"choices":[{"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Auto-refresh is subscriber-driven. The "},{"code":".task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier in "},{"code":"DiceView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cancels when the view disappears, removing the last subscriber from "},{"code":"lastRoll.values","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". With no subscribers, the timer stops — no manual cleanup is needed."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer stops automatically because there are no more subscribers."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer is subscriber-driven, not a free-running background process. It only runs while at least one subscriber is active on the "},{"code":"values","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" stream."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer keeps running in the background indefinitely."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No manual invalidation is needed. Silo tracks the subscriber count automatically and stops the timer when it reaches zero."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer stops, but only if you call "},{"code":"invalidate()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on the "},{"code":"DiceRoller","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"multiple-choice"}],"anchor":"Check-Your-Understanding"},{"kind":"callToAction","title":"Reacting to Dice Configuration","action":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies","isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"Get started","type":"text"}],"type":"reference","overridingTitle":"Get started"},"abstract":[{"text":"Build a configurable dice roller that automatically re-rolls whenever the player changes the dice type or count. You will learn how to declare dependencies, choose the right refresh policy, and wire SwiftUI pickers to reactive streams — resulting in a fully functional application.","type":"text"}],"featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller"},"references":{"doc://Silo/tutorials/Silo/ReactiveDependencies#Adding-a-Second-Dependency":{"title":"Adding a Second Dependency","kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol","url":"\/tutorials\/silo\/reactivedependencies#Adding-a-Second-Dependency","abstract":[{"text":"Build a configurable dice roller that automatically re-rolls whenever the player changes the dice type or count. You will learn how to declare dependencies, choose the right refresh policy, and wire SwiftUI pickers to reactive streams — resulting in a fully functional application.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Adding-a-Second-Dependency","type":"section"},"doc://Silo/tutorials/Silo/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Rolling-Automatically":{"title":"Rolling Automatically","kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol","url":"\/tutorials\/silo\/buildingad6diceroller#Rolling-Automatically","abstract":[{"text":"In this tutorial, you will build a D6 dice roller using Silo. The fetch is a single line — ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int.random(in: 1...6)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — so every concept you encounter is focused on Silo, with no boilerplate distractions.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Rolling-Automatically","type":"section"},"DiceView-02.png":{"identifier":"DiceView-02.png","variants":[{"traits":["1x","light"],"url":"\/images\/Silo\/DiceView-02.png"}],"alt":"Dice view showing a dash before the first roll","type":"image"},"doc://Silo/tutorials/Silo/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Check-Your-Understanding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Check-Your-Understanding","title":"Check Your Understanding","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Check Your Understanding","type":"text"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/silo\/buildingad6diceroller#Check-Your-Understanding","type":"link"},"doc://Silo/tutorials/Silo/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Building-the-Dice-View":{"abstract":[{"text":"In this tutorial, you will build a D6 dice roller using Silo. The fetch is a single line — ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int.random(in: 1...6)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — so every concept you encounter is focused on Silo, with no boilerplate distractions.","type":"text"}],"type":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Building-the-Dice-View","title":"Building the Dice View","url":"\/tutorials\/silo\/buildingad6diceroller#Building-the-Dice-View","kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"doc://Silo/tutorials/Silo/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Creating-the-Data-Source":{"abstract":[{"text":"In this tutorial, you will build a D6 dice roller using Silo. The fetch is a single line — ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int.random(in: 1...6)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — so every concept you encounter is focused on Silo, with no boilerplate distractions.","type":"text"}],"type":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Creating-the-Data-Source","title":"Creating the Data Source","url":"\/tutorials\/silo\/buildingad6diceroller#Creating-the-Data-Source","kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"DiceRoller-03.swift":{"type":"file","identifier":"DiceRoller-03.swift","content":["import Silo","","@MainActor","class DiceRoller {","    static let shared = DiceRoller()","","    let lastRoll: DataSource<Int?>","","    private init() {","        lastRoll = dataSource {","            try? await Task.sleep(for: .seconds(1))","            return Int.random(in: 1...6)","        } onError: { _ in","            .keep","        }","        .autoRefresh(.seconds(2))","        .build()","    }","}"],"fileName":"DiceRoller.swift","syntax":"swift","fileType":"swift","highlights":[]},"doc://Silo/tutorials/Silo/ReactiveDependencies#Check-Your-Understanding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/t